    {
      "id": "claim_17771dbd6ce243f1b942a58c6981b746",
      "statement": "A PPH wire moves through seven processing stages in order: Intake, Validation & enrichment, Screening (synchronous PRSP SanctionScreen/Sentinel call; a hit creates an HMS hold and moves the payment to HELD), Funds control (memo debit against CDP; insufficient funds create HRC-05 holds with auto-retry until 5:30 p.m. ET), Release (UETR assigned, pacs.008/pacs.009 built), Network (sent to Fedwire Funds Connector or Swift Alliance/gpi Connector), and Close (accounting close to COMPLETED; later pacs.004 returns transition the wire to RETURNED).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pph-sys-ovw-9.2-prism-payments-hub-system-overview-and-lifecycle-state-model.md#L38-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f639c914bd212446bd1d2c5d4313d61e968875b18c65594496368e5e87c7aa7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_da0ca2707e3c4fd79eddf377ffd29d35",
      "statement": "PPH-SYS-OVW-9.2 defines the canonical thirteen-state PPH v2 wire lifecycle (RECEIVED, VALIDATING, SCREENING, HELD, REPAIR, FUNDS_CONTROL, WAREHOUSED, RELEASED, SENT_TO_NETWORK, NETWORK_ACCEPTED, NETWORK_REJECTED, COMPLETED, CANCELLED, RETURNED) together with the v1 status value each state is shown as, and documents that v1 collapses RELEASED, SENT_TO_NETWORK, NETWORK_ACCEPTED, and COMPLETED into the single v1 value PROCESSED.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pph-sys-ovw-9.2-prism-payments-hub-system-overview-and-lifecycle-state-model.md#L54-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bde107894ff96b385e7ce3462c846a6a6c16cc21f3e0a22fa2e5c8c6d84c8dbf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_05b7a14532fb43fb8cd02807129a29f2",
      "statement": "NETWORK_ACCEPTED has rail-specific business meaning: for Fedwire Funds it is the Federal Reserve's pacs.002 positive acknowledgment carrying the OMAD, representing final and irrevocable interbank settlement under Regulation J/UCC Article 4A without confirming beneficiary credit; for Swift CBPR+ it is only a SwiftNet delivery ACK for pacs.008 with no settlement implication, with beneficiary credit knowable only via a Swift gpi ACCC status. The v2 stateHistory timestamp for NETWORK_ACCEPTED is PPH's processing time, not the Federal Reserve's pacs.002 creation timestamp, which travels separately on net.fedwire.ack.v1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pph-sys-ovw-9.2-prism-payments-hub-system-overview-and-lifecycle-state-model.md#L88-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0e075ddaf74fe14ef25d7654439b547f620a93a40fb689563c40fbfb4f7605d8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e0494c85993d490592adcbb857d4b0f8",
      "statement": "PPH-SYS-OVW-9.2 scopes six payment identifiers and their interface availability: pphId (PPH-assigned internal key, v1/v2/events), cboRef (CBO-assigned channel reference, v2 identifiers.cboRef only when channel=CBO), IMAD (PPH-assigned Fedwire sender id, v1 fedRef and v2 identifiers.imad), OMAD (Federal Reserve-assigned, v2 identifiers.omad and net.fedwire.ack.v1 only, absent from v1), UETR (PPH-assigned at release, v2 identifiers.uetr and lifecycle v2 events), and EndToEndId (originator/PPH, v2 only).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pph-sys-ovw-9.2-prism-payments-hub-system-overview-and-lifecycle-state-model.md#L97-L106",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea23ef2c4f42c936de062beca162eac894af0795b48f20c49f8f94b6a6e64f84:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_87c149140f4643faa1171dea3bd22ef5",
      "statement": "When screening or funds control raises a hold, HMS returns a holdId and PPH transitions the payment to HELD; since a 2019 integration PPH also synchronizes the HMS hold's free-text description into the legacy v1 field holdReasonDesc for Wire Room console backward compatibility, while the v2 API exposes only hold.isHeld and hold.holdId per ADR-PAY-021.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pph-sys-ovw-9.2-prism-payments-hub-system-overview-and-lifecycle-state-model.md#L108-L110",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fa0c1a110c0ec2463fb4a9a90e31befc095af4f57c313f725a2fbcc597d1b9f9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1777930ddcd94d11baaeffad0c42cb75",
      "statement": "PPH-SYS-OVW-9.2 specifies PPH's operating cutoffs: the Fedwire operating day runs 9:00 p.m. ET (prior calendar day) to 7:00 p.m. ET, the Fedwire third-party customer transfer cutoff is 6:00 p.m. ET (later items warehoused under HRC-04), the CBO same-day domestic wire cutoff is 5:30 p.m. ET, and international cutoffs vary by currency (e.g., EUR 2:00 p.m. ET, GBP 1:00 p.m. ET, MXN 3:00 p.m. ET, JPY prior day).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pph-sys-ovw-9.2-prism-payments-hub-system-overview-and-lifecycle-state-model.md#L112-L130",
